# .env — where passwords and API keys live, and NOWHERE else.
#
# Rules (Claude enforces these too):
#   - Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values only when a project needs one.
#   - Never paste a key into the chat, an email, or any other file.
#   - This file never leaves this computer and never goes into git.
#   - If Brady hands you a key for something, it goes here, one line, like below.
#
# Examples (fake values — replace when you actually need one):
# SOME_SERVICE_API_KEY=paste-the-key-here

# --- Social dashboard (projects/social-dashboard) ---
# YouTube: fill the first two from Google Cloud (see CONNECT_YOUTUBE.md).
# The third is filled in automatically by connect_youtube.py.
YT_CLIENT_ID=
YT_CLIENT_SECRET=
YT_REFRESH_TOKEN=
